WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.733 --> 00:00:04.066
Continuing their journey to Shalour City

2
00:00:04.133 --> 00:00:05.966
and Ash's third Gym battle challenge,

3
00:00:06.033 --> 00:00:09.966
our heroes seem to have wandered into an all-too-familiar situation.

4
00:00:10.033 --> 00:00:13.633
- Pika! Pi!
- Catching Pikachu is meant to be!

5
00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:16.000
- Inkay, help them agree!
- Inkay!

6
00:00:16.066 --> 00:00:20.000
You're never going to get away with it! Froakie, I choose you!

7
00:00:21.599 --> 00:00:23.900
- Froakie!
- Froakie, Water Pulse!

8
00:00:23.966 --> 00:00:27.033
Froakie!

9
00:00:27.099 --> 00:00:29.766
-Dodge it!

10
00:00:29.833 --> 00:00:32.000
- I've got just the thing!
- Huh?

11
00:00:32.066 --> 00:00:36.733
The future is now, thanks to science! Clemontic Gear on!

12
00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:38.800
- Huh?
- Clemont, what's that?

13
00:00:38.866 --> 00:00:40.733
Just watch this and you'll see!

14
00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:42.000
Inkay, Psybeam!

15
00:00:42.066 --> 00:00:45.199
Inkay!

16
00:00:46.433 --> 00:00:47.866
- Oh!
- Oh, my!

17
00:00:47.933 --> 00:00:52.466
I call it my Mechanical Absorption of Any Pokémon's Move!

18
00:00:52.533 --> 00:00:54.166
The name needs work.

19
00:00:54.233 --> 00:00:58.566
- All right, use Tackle!
- Inkay!

20
00:00:58.633 --> 00:01:01.166
You see? It works for physical attacks as well!

21
00:01:01.233 --> 00:01:05.133
Oh, man, science is so amazing! Okay, Froakie, use Bubble!

22
00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:10.066
Froakie!

23
00:01:10.133 --> 00:01:12.733
Oh! Pumpkaboo, use Shadow Ball!

24
00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:15.000
Pumpkaboo!

25
00:01:16.533 --> 00:01:18.600
- It's working well!
- Dark Pulse, go!

26
00:01:21.433 --> 00:01:22.933
- Oh!
- Use Water Pulse!

27
00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:25.833
Froakie!

28
00:01:25.899 --> 00:01:28.433
-Pika!

29
00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:33.766
- Pikachu, use Thunderbolt!
- Pikachu!

30
00:01:34.766 --> 00:01:37.399
We're blasting off again!

31
00:01:39.833 --> 00:01:41.666
Clemont, you did it!

32
00:01:41.733 --> 00:01:43.233
Your invention is great!

33
00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:45.266
Ha-ha! Hey Clemont, thanks a lot!

34
00:01:45.333 --> 00:01:49.066
You're welcome! Although it's still in the prototype stage,

35
00:01:49.133 --> 00:01:51.000
I have a good feeling... Huh?

36
00:01:56.533 --> 00:01:59.000
I guess it's back to the old drawing board.

37
00:02:03.133 --> 00:02:05.133
We were so close to catching Pikachu!

38
00:02:05.199 --> 00:02:07.899
So close times zero still equals zero.

39
00:02:07.966 --> 00:02:09.266
It's just not fair!

40
00:02:09.333 --> 00:02:12.266
How do we compete against an absurd twerp invention?

41
00:02:12.333 --> 00:02:14.766
Why try to compete when we can steal?

42
00:02:14.833 --> 00:02:19.533
Ah! Utilizing that move-absorbing device would be nice!

43
00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:22.133
But we first need a strategy and I've got it!

44
00:02:24.566 --> 00:02:26.466
Now that's what I call a plan!

45
00:02:26.533 --> 00:02:28.066
But how do we execute?

46
00:02:28.133 --> 00:02:31.266
You just have faith in my acting expertise

47
00:02:31.333 --> 00:02:33.933
And the rest of it will be a breeze!

48
00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:36.799
♪ I want to be the very best ♪

49
00:02:36.866 --> 00:02:40.533
♪ Like no one ever was ♪

50
00:02:40.600 --> 00:02:43.299
♪ To catch them is my real test ♪

51
00:02:43.366 --> 00:02:46.233
♪ To train them is my cause ♪

52
00:02:46.299 --> 00:02:49.299
♪ Pokémon! Got to catch them all It's you and me ♪

53
00:02:49.366 --> 00:02:52.566
♪ Pokémon! I know it's my destiny ♪

54
00:02:52.633 --> 00:02:55.933
♪ Pokémon! Yeah, you're my best friend ♪

55
00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:58.366
♪ In a world we must defend ♪

56
00:02:58.433 --> 00:03:00.933
♪ Pokémon! Got to catch them all ♪

57
00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:04.000
♪ Got to catch them all! Pokémon! ♪

58
00:03:13.700 --> 00:03:16.833
That's it, Pancham! Great!

59
00:03:16.899 --> 00:03:20.333
- Hey! That's a Pancham, isn't it?
- That's right.

60
00:03:20.399 --> 00:03:25.533
Hi! The name's Ash and I came all the way here from Pallet Town!

61
00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:27.766
Well, I come from here and I'm Myron!

62
00:03:27.833 --> 00:03:31.033
Hey, Serena and Bonnie, check it out! There's a Pancham over here!

63
00:03:31.100 --> 00:03:33.100
Hi!

64
00:03:34.100 --> 00:03:36.399
I'm Serena, from Vaniville Town!

65
00:03:36.466 --> 00:03:38.399
I'm Bonnie, from Lumiose City!

66
00:03:38.466 --> 00:03:41.133
This is my cute friend Dedenne! Na-na! Na-na!

67
00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:43.733
And this is my partner, Pikachu!

68
00:03:43.799 --> 00:03:46.133
Huh? Your Pikachu can float in the air?

69
00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:48.366
That's from lots of special training!

70
00:03:48.433 --> 00:03:51.366
- Awesome, huh? My buddy!
- Inkay! Inkay!

71
00:03:51.433 --> 00:03:54.399
Huh? I didn't know a Pikachu sounded like that.

72
00:03:54.466 --> 00:03:57.600
Now you do! So let's have a battle!

73
00:03:57.666 --> 00:04:02.799
Battle? No way! I really don't want to put Pancham in a battle!

74
00:04:02.866 --> 00:04:05.666
Having a battle's awesome! So what do you say?

75
00:04:05.733 --> 00:04:07.366
Okay, Pikachu, use Psybeam!

76
00:04:07.433 --> 00:04:09.899
Pika!

77
00:04:12.166 --> 00:04:16.066
Oh! Now how could your Pikachu know how to use Psybeam?

78
00:04:16.133 --> 00:04:18.666
We train hard! Now, Tackle!

79
00:04:21.533 --> 00:04:25.933
Pancham! Uh! Are you okay? Stop it, already!

80
00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:30.099
Ah! What a bore having a battle with a weak Pancham!

81
00:04:30.166 --> 00:04:32.466
We should go before I fall asleep.

82
00:04:32.533 --> 00:04:36.033
That's too bad. Ever seen anything so uncute?

83
00:04:36.099 --> 00:04:38.566
Na-na! Na! Na-na-na-na!

84
00:04:38.633 --> 00:04:41.400
I'm going to tell Officer Jenny!

85
00:04:41.466 --> 00:04:42.599
Here you go!

86
00:04:45.599 --> 00:04:48.099
- Bye-bye.
- Hey, you didn't pay for anything!

87
00:04:48.166 --> 00:04:50.000
That's 'cause I'm Ash from Pallet Town!

88
00:04:50.066 --> 00:04:51.733
And I'm Serena from Vaniville Town!

89
00:04:51.800 --> 00:04:54.366
And I'm cute Bonnie from Lumiose City!

90
00:04:55.833 --> 00:04:57.333
Hey! Where's my money?

91
00:04:57.400 --> 00:05:00.133
In our pockets! Says Serena from Vaniville Town!

92
00:05:00.200 --> 00:05:01.833
And Ash from Pallet Town!

93
00:05:01.900 --> 00:05:04.433
And Bonnie from Lumiose City! Cute!

94
00:05:04.500 --> 00:05:08.566
The nerve! How dare they run after eating and drinking so much!

95
00:05:11.333 --> 00:05:14.466
- Finally! We're in town.
- Pika.

96
00:05:14.533 --> 00:05:17.066
- I told Officer Jenny about you!
- Huh?

97
00:05:17.133 --> 00:05:21.166
That's weird. How come your Pikachu isn't floating in the air like before?

98
00:05:21.233 --> 00:05:22.599
Floating?

99
00:05:22.666 --> 00:05:25.666
I'm really sorry! I thought you were Ash from Pallet Town!

100
00:05:25.733 --> 00:05:29.099
- Hey, what's going on here? Huh?
- Pika?

101
00:05:29.166 --> 00:05:33.033
Now, look, you kids ordered all that food and then you ate every bit of it!

102
00:05:33.099 --> 00:05:36.000
You owe me a lot of money, you know.

103
00:05:36.066 --> 00:05:38.766
Wait. We just got into town this minute, sir!

104
00:05:38.833 --> 00:05:41.733
- We haven't eaten anything!
- He's right!

105
00:05:41.800 --> 00:05:44.266
Hold on, you do seem different now.

106
00:05:44.333 --> 00:05:47.766
- Yeah. I think you made a mistake.
- I'm sorry.

107
00:05:50.766 --> 00:05:52.566
Everyone's feeling better now.

108
00:05:52.633 --> 00:05:54.266
Thanks so much, Nurse Joy!

109
00:05:54.333 --> 00:05:57.033
Attention, please. Ash from Pallet Town,

110
00:05:57.099 --> 00:06:00.833
Serena from Vaniville Town and Bonnie from Lumiose City,

111
00:06:00.900 --> 00:06:03.000
please come to the Pokémon Center entrance.

112
00:06:03.066 --> 00:06:04.266
What for?

113
00:06:05.233 --> 00:06:09.333
- Huh?
- Uh! Ah, there you are!

114
00:06:09.400 --> 00:06:12.866
It's time for you guys to pay your bill already!

115
00:06:12.933 --> 00:06:16.133
Hold on! We just got into town. It's our first time here!

116
00:06:16.200 --> 00:06:17.366
Pikachu.

117
00:06:17.433 --> 00:06:19.733
Are you sure these are the ones?

118
00:06:19.799 --> 00:06:22.633
I don't know. They're all dressed the same.

119
00:06:22.700 --> 00:06:24.866
You're Ash from Pallet Town, correct?

120
00:06:24.933 --> 00:06:27.233
- Right!
- And you're Pikachu, right?

121
00:06:27.299 --> 00:06:28.599
Pikachu!

122
00:06:28.666 --> 00:06:30.599
And you're Serena from Vaniville Town?

123
00:06:30.666 --> 00:06:32.200
- Yes, I am!
- You?

124
00:06:32.266 --> 00:06:35.200
You must be Bonnie from Lumiose City

125
00:06:35.266 --> 00:06:38.400
and I'll bet Dedenne must be in your bag.

126
00:06:38.466 --> 00:06:39.700
Na-na!

127
00:06:39.766 --> 00:06:43.200
I'd be very interested to hear what you all have to say.

128
00:06:43.266 --> 00:06:45.966
You might be involved in some kind of trouble.

129
00:06:46.033 --> 00:06:47.933
Sure, no problem!

130
00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:49.700
What about me?

131
00:06:49.766 --> 00:06:52.433
Wait for us in the lobby! We'll call when we're done!

132
00:06:52.500 --> 00:06:55.433
Uh, okay.

133
00:06:55.500 --> 00:06:57.799
I'm so confused.

134
00:07:01.933 --> 00:07:04.233
Part one of our plan is a success.

135
00:07:04.299 --> 00:07:07.366
We've separated the inventor twerp from the rest of the twerps.

136
00:07:07.433 --> 00:07:11.433
Plus we got to feed and refeed our faces. Double prizes!

137
00:07:11.500 --> 00:07:15.566
That's our Jess, the most devious mind on the devious planet!

138
00:07:15.633 --> 00:07:18.666
Now it's time for part two to get under way.

139
00:07:18.733 --> 00:07:20.066
Yay!

140
00:07:20.133 --> 00:07:23.366
What? -Fakes in this town?

141
00:07:23.433 --> 00:07:25.466
Forcing people to battle?

142
00:07:25.533 --> 00:07:28.533
Eating and drinking a lot and then running without paying?

143
00:07:28.599 --> 00:07:32.366
That's right and when they run away, they announce your names to everybody!

144
00:07:32.433 --> 00:07:36.400
So I asked you to come here to see if you knew what's been going on.

145
00:07:36.466 --> 00:07:39.400
This photo is from the restaurant's surveillance camera.

146
00:07:39.466 --> 00:07:42.566
- They do look like us.
- Yeah, but why?

147
00:07:42.633 --> 00:07:46.066
We have no idea, but we're currently investigating.

148
00:07:46.133 --> 00:07:50.233
So I'm asking you to please be extra careful during your stay here!

149
00:07:50.299 --> 00:07:53.533
- That's all for now. You can go.
- Thanks.

150
00:07:54.500 --> 00:07:57.033
There are some weird people in town disguised as us!

151
00:07:57.099 --> 00:08:01.866
I'm so mad at them! We'll tell you a lot more when we get back! See you!

152
00:08:04.200 --> 00:08:07.033
I wonder why there wasn't anyone pretending to be my brother.

153
00:08:07.099 --> 00:08:09.200
- That's weird!
- Yeah, you're right.

154
00:08:09.266 --> 00:08:12.166
- It makes no sense to me.
- Pika.

155
00:08:12.233 --> 00:08:15.599
I can't believe how odd that is.

156
00:08:15.666 --> 00:08:19.166
Excuse us, but are you that brilliant young inventor, Clemont?

157
00:08:19.233 --> 00:08:21.333
Uh, brilliant? Well...

158
00:08:21.400 --> 00:08:24.533
Allow us to introduce ourselves.

159
00:08:24.599 --> 00:08:28.166
You're from the Kalos Institute of Technology? Oh.

160
00:08:28.233 --> 00:08:32.933
We're in the process of building an important device, but we need your help.

161
00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:37.100
If we're going to succeed, input from a genius like you is critical!

162
00:08:37.166 --> 00:08:39.133
- Like me?
- Of course!

163
00:08:39.199 --> 00:08:43.400
We've heard all about you, how unique and revolutionary your inventions are.

164
00:08:43.466 --> 00:08:46.833
People in the know are saying they're brilliant and incredibly useful!

165
00:08:46.900 --> 00:08:48.666
Hm! Yes, indeed!

166
00:08:48.733 --> 00:08:51.266
Brilliant enough to figuratively blind you.

167
00:08:51.333 --> 00:08:53.166
Devices from the future!

168
00:08:53.233 --> 00:08:57.666
- Works from a master inventor!
- You're embarrassing me!

169
00:08:57.733 --> 00:09:00.733
Please, Clemont, sir, work alongside us!

170
00:09:00.800 --> 00:09:03.400
I'll help in any way I can!

171
00:09:03.466 --> 00:09:07.800
I have an important job to do so I'll be going out for a while.

172
00:09:07.866 --> 00:09:09.733
Please don't wait for me to have dinner.

173
00:09:09.800 --> 00:09:12.933
I'll be back later this evening. Clemont.

174
00:09:13.000 --> 00:09:14.733
Would you give this to Ash, please?

175
00:09:16.866 --> 00:09:18.266
Yes, of course!

176
00:09:18.333 --> 00:09:22.733
Incredible! You've got all sorts of equipment.

177
00:09:22.800 --> 00:09:25.666
- Do you mind if I examine it?
- Not at all!

178
00:09:25.733 --> 00:09:30.666
Wow! A complete set of tools! This is so exciting!

179
00:09:30.733 --> 00:09:32.666
Here's what we're working on!

180
00:09:32.733 --> 00:09:38.833
- Behold!
- Wow! A Heliolisk robot? Fantastic!

181
00:09:38.900 --> 00:09:41.766
Oh! This is as far as we've gotten.

182
00:09:41.833 --> 00:09:43.333
We were commissioned to build it

183
00:09:43.400 --> 00:09:46.199
by an organization dedicated to world peace.

184
00:09:46.266 --> 00:09:50.666
But a cruel, nasty Electric-type Pokémon continues to sabotage our work!

185
00:09:50.733 --> 00:09:52.766
That's not very nice.

186
00:09:52.833 --> 00:09:58.300
And so we humbly request that you build us an Electric-type defensive device.

187
00:09:58.366 --> 00:10:03.333
Hm! Electric-type defensive device, eh?

188
00:10:03.400 --> 00:10:05.233
Well?

189
00:10:05.300 --> 00:10:07.133
Yes! That will be a breeze!

190
00:10:07.199 --> 00:10:09.866
Joy! We knew we could count on you!

191
00:10:09.933 --> 00:10:13.633
First off, I'll need to gather a number of insulating materials.

192
00:10:13.699 --> 00:10:16.166
Let's get started right away!

193
00:10:16.233 --> 00:10:19.566
It will be hard to move if too much electricity builds up,

194
00:10:19.633 --> 00:10:22.666
so I'll need to install a discharge mechanism as well.

195
00:10:22.733 --> 00:10:25.733
You are a true genius, Clemont!

196
00:10:25.800 --> 00:10:28.100
We never would've thought of that!

197
00:10:28.166 --> 00:10:32.666
This goes here. Then I do this...

198
00:10:37.166 --> 00:10:39.000
Your Kalos region update?

199
00:10:39.066 --> 00:10:42.900
Sir, we now have two Pokémon. Pumpkaboo.

200
00:10:42.966 --> 00:10:44.966
And Inkay.

201
00:10:45.033 --> 00:10:46.500
I'm quite happy to hear that.

202
00:10:46.566 --> 00:10:50.966
We're working hard to increase our firepower by catching more Pokémon.

203
00:10:51.033 --> 00:10:54.500
And soon, you'll be receiving even more exciting news from us!

204
00:10:54.566 --> 00:10:56.600
I look forward to that.

205
00:10:57.566 --> 00:10:59.400
We'll do our best. We simply must!

206
00:10:59.466 --> 00:11:01.833
We'll get Pikachu this time or bust!

207
00:11:01.900 --> 00:11:04.199
Wobbuffet!

208
00:11:04.266 --> 00:11:06.733
Who's that Pokémon?

209
00:11:11.066 --> 00:11:13.066
It's Inkay!

210
00:11:17.066 --> 00:11:18.733
Finished. Perfect!

211
00:11:18.800 --> 00:11:22.466
- Bravo, Clemont!
- Excellent effort!

212
00:11:22.533 --> 00:11:26.433
We would be honored if you would name this for us, brilliant lad.

213
00:11:27.433 --> 00:11:29.266
Hm. Let's see.

214
00:11:29.333 --> 00:11:33.066
How about the Electricity Has No Effect on Me-a-Tron?

215
00:11:33.133 --> 00:11:36.000
- Big fail.
- Hey, what's that?

216
00:11:37.199 --> 00:11:40.699
Initially, we thought we'd build a Pokémon transport machine.

217
00:11:40.766 --> 00:11:43.400
But we couldn't get the thing to work!

218
00:11:44.733 --> 00:11:48.400
As the capsule travels through the tube, it get stuck.

219
00:11:48.466 --> 00:11:52.500
- Huh. I could see if I can adjust it.
- Really?

220
00:11:54.366 --> 00:11:56.866
Of course! How far do you want to send the capsule?

221
00:11:56.933 --> 00:11:59.100
One and a half miles or so.

222
00:11:59.166 --> 00:12:00.733
One and a half miles.

223
00:12:00.800 --> 00:12:03.600
If the capsule with a Pokémon in it weighs this

224
00:12:03.666 --> 00:12:06.199
and if the distance is one and a half miles,

225
00:12:06.266 --> 00:12:08.733
then the necessary output would have to be...

226
00:12:08.800 --> 00:12:11.100
All right, I've got it!

227
00:12:11.166 --> 00:12:15.866
It's all done. Now we seal it, so we can increase the pressure.

228
00:12:20.699 --> 00:12:22.733
Adjustment complete!

229
00:12:22.800 --> 00:12:25.400
Bravo! Bravissimo, Clemont!

230
00:12:25.466 --> 00:12:27.199
We are humbled by your greatness.

231
00:12:28.166 --> 00:12:30.300
I can't thank you enough for all your help!

232
00:12:30.366 --> 00:12:33.866
Glad I could be of service. Thanks!

233
00:12:33.933 --> 00:12:35.599
Huh? Oh!

234
00:12:36.599 --> 00:12:39.066
Where could Clemont have gone off to?

235
00:12:39.133 --> 00:12:40.766
- I'm back!
- Huh?

236
00:12:40.833 --> 00:12:42.833
Clemont, where have you been?

237
00:12:42.900 --> 00:12:46.900
A couple of scientists asked me to help assist them with several of their machines

238
00:12:46.966 --> 00:12:49.266
they were having a bit of trouble with.

239
00:12:49.333 --> 00:12:52.266
So, what was Officer Jenny talking about?

240
00:12:52.333 --> 00:12:54.633
Some people are pretending to be us!

241
00:12:54.699 --> 00:12:57.000
They go around telling everybody our names.

242
00:12:57.066 --> 00:12:58.433
Pika! Pika!

243
00:12:58.500 --> 00:13:02.666
And whoever's pretending to be me even has a bag with a Dedenne inside!

244
00:13:02.733 --> 00:13:05.333
- Na-na-na!
- Someone's pretending to be me too!

245
00:13:05.400 --> 00:13:07.133
Fakes of all three of you?

246
00:13:07.199 --> 00:13:09.500
We have to find out who they are, quick!

247
00:13:09.566 --> 00:13:12.333
That's right! I can't take it much longer!

248
00:13:12.400 --> 00:13:16.566
I'm not going to let them drag our names through the mud like this anymore!

249
00:13:18.633 --> 00:13:20.933
Everything's safely buried now!

250
00:13:21.000 --> 00:13:23.533
Tomorrow's going to be a lot of fun.

251
00:13:26.966 --> 00:13:29.966
-Come back here!

252
00:13:30.033 --> 00:13:31.533
You forgot to pay for your food!

253
00:13:31.599 --> 00:13:33.266
So? I'm Ash from Pallet Town!

254
00:13:33.333 --> 00:13:35.166
And I'm Serena from Vaniville Town!

255
00:13:35.233 --> 00:13:37.533
I'm Bonnie from Lumiose City!

256
00:13:39.233 --> 00:13:42.133
Once the twerps learn there are copies of them running around,

257
00:13:42.199 --> 00:13:45.733
they're going to want to stop us and that's when we lure them into our trap!

258
00:13:45.800 --> 00:13:48.266
- It's a snap!
- It tickles my cap!

259
00:13:48.333 --> 00:13:50.266
Were there people here who look like us?

260
00:13:50.333 --> 00:13:53.333
Yeah and they ate without paying me anything!

261
00:13:53.400 --> 00:13:55.266
Do you know which way they went?

262
00:13:55.333 --> 00:13:57.500
Hm. They took off over in that direction.

263
00:13:57.566 --> 00:13:59.266
Thanks a lot!

264
00:14:02.400 --> 00:14:05.900
Got to find those fakes! There!

265
00:14:05.966 --> 00:14:08.199
- Oh, hello!
- You're the ones!

266
00:14:08.266 --> 00:14:10.966
- Who are you?
- Your clothes are awful!

267
00:14:11.033 --> 00:14:13.733
- Not like mine at all!
- Ta-da!

268
00:14:13.800 --> 00:14:16.066
- Ah! I never say ta-da!!
- Ta-da, ta-da, ta-da!

269
00:14:16.133 --> 00:14:18.066
I don't do that ever!

270
00:14:18.133 --> 00:14:22.466
It wasn't easy for me to dress down with no class, like you do.

271
00:14:22.533 --> 00:14:24.066
What was that?

272
00:14:24.133 --> 00:14:27.033
And I truly detested acting like a total buffoon.

273
00:14:27.099 --> 00:14:28.466
What?

274
00:14:28.533 --> 00:14:31.066
- Right, Pikachu?
- Intay!

275
00:14:31.133 --> 00:14:35.933
Huh? Huh? Come on, you're not Pikachu!

276
00:14:36.000 --> 00:14:38.533
And you're not even a little bit cute!

277
00:14:38.599 --> 00:14:41.133
- Na-na-na!
- That's a puppet!

278
00:14:41.199 --> 00:14:42.433
Na-na!

279
00:14:44.733 --> 00:14:47.433
Prepare for trouble, without our disguises!

280
00:14:47.500 --> 00:14:49.666
And make it double, with no surprises!

281
00:14:49.733 --> 00:14:52.166
To protect the world from devastation!

282
00:14:52.233 --> 00:14:55.266
To unite all people within our nation!

283
00:14:55.333 --> 00:14:57.800
To denounce the evils truth and love!

284
00:14:57.866 --> 00:15:01.566
To extend our reach to the stars above!

285
00:15:01.633 --> 00:15:03.900
- Jessie!
- And James!

286
00:15:03.966 --> 00:15:06.900
Team Rocket rips you off at the speed of light!

287
00:15:06.966 --> 00:15:09.733
Surrender now or prepare for a fraudulent fight!

288
00:15:09.800 --> 00:15:13.166
- Meowth, that's right!
- Wobbuffet!

289
00:15:14.533 --> 00:15:15.599
Team Rocket!

290
00:15:15.666 --> 00:15:17.966
Why were you pretending to be us?

291
00:15:18.033 --> 00:15:21.599
Obviously your twerpish brains don't work that well, so we'll tell you.

292
00:15:21.666 --> 00:15:24.233
Team Rocket's future is now, thanks to science!

293
00:15:24.300 --> 00:15:27.133
Team Rocketronic Gear on!

294
00:15:29.000 --> 00:15:31.000
Ah!

295
00:15:32.599 --> 00:15:35.733
- Oh!
- I worked on that robot!

296
00:15:35.800 --> 00:15:38.900
You can't unring a bell and you did your work so well!

297
00:15:38.966 --> 00:15:42.266
- No! What have I done?
- Thank you for your brilliant help.

298
00:15:42.333 --> 00:15:44.533
Without your naïve assistance, we'd be lost.

299
00:15:44.599 --> 00:15:49.033
So they were the scientists that asked you to go help them out with their robots!

300
00:15:49.099 --> 00:15:53.533
Right! And disguising ourselves as you to separate him from you was the goal!

301
00:15:53.599 --> 00:15:56.400
And as you can see, it worked out inventively well!

302
00:15:56.466 --> 00:15:59.400
-Pikachu!

303
00:15:59.466 --> 00:16:01.833
Today is the day we catch Pikachu for sure,

304
00:16:01.900 --> 00:16:05.400
with our Electricity Has No Effect on Me-a-Tron!

305
00:16:05.466 --> 00:16:07.033
That's a bad name.

306
00:16:07.099 --> 00:16:09.066
Yeah, I have to agree.

307
00:16:09.133 --> 00:16:12.466
You can thank your brilliant Clemont for that unique name!

308
00:16:12.533 --> 00:16:17.066
- You did it?
- No! The agony! The shame!

309
00:16:17.133 --> 00:16:20.400
One Pikachu, coming up!

310
00:16:20.466 --> 00:16:22.233
- Dodge!
- Pika!

311
00:16:22.300 --> 00:16:27.000
- Use Thunderbolt!
- Pikachu!

312
00:16:27.066 --> 00:16:29.000
Clemont's idea was pure genius!

313
00:16:29.066 --> 00:16:31.266
With multiple layers of insulation,

314
00:16:31.333 --> 00:16:34.466
the anti-Electric-type device works like a charm!

315
00:16:34.533 --> 00:16:39.533
Ah. I had no idea Pikachu was the cruel, nasty Electric-type Pokémon!

316
00:16:39.599 --> 00:16:44.300
- Use Electro Ball!
- Pika! Pika! Pika! Pik!

317
00:16:45.466 --> 00:16:48.633
Hm. Show them how!

318
00:16:50.866 --> 00:16:53.866
Pika!

319
00:16:53.933 --> 00:16:59.599
- Pikachu!
- Pika! Pika!

320
00:16:59.666 --> 00:17:01.500
Whee! Got you!

321
00:17:01.566 --> 00:17:03.566
Now what?

322
00:17:03.633 --> 00:17:05.933
- What's that?
- Our Pokémon transport machine!

323
00:17:06.000 --> 00:17:08.599
- Oh!
- You can thank Clemont for this, too!

324
00:17:09.833 --> 00:17:13.133
- And go!
- No! Pikachu!

325
00:17:15.233 --> 00:17:19.033
That's not music to my ears. What's the problem?

326
00:17:19.099 --> 00:17:21.566
The problem is my big brother made it.

327
00:17:21.633 --> 00:17:23.933
Everybody, get down!

328
00:17:26.099 --> 00:17:29.466
- The robot went blooey!
- But we have Pikachu!

329
00:17:29.533 --> 00:17:31.533
'Cause our plan worked, like it should!

330
00:17:31.600 --> 00:17:35.600
- Life is good!
- Wobbuffet!

331
00:17:38.433 --> 00:17:41.800
Pikachu! Pikachu!

332
00:17:41.866 --> 00:17:43.100
Where did it go?

333
00:17:43.166 --> 00:17:45.766
Clemont, put me in a capsule and send me off after them!

334
00:17:45.833 --> 00:17:50.000
The capsule was designed for Pokémon only and besides, there's just one!

335
00:17:50.066 --> 00:17:52.766
- All right, then!
- Ash! It won't work!

336
00:17:52.833 --> 00:17:55.966
Wait a minute! I know what to do.

337
00:17:56.033 --> 00:17:58.000
What are you thinking about?

338
00:17:58.066 --> 00:18:01.266
- Serena, I'd like to use your guidebook.
- Here.

339
00:18:01.333 --> 00:18:05.733
Now, Team Rocket told me they wanted to transfer a Pokémon one and a half miles.

340
00:18:05.800 --> 00:18:09.166
- So what?
- Look, we're here on the map.

341
00:18:09.233 --> 00:18:12.100
So the other end of the transport machine has to be somewhere

342
00:18:12.166 --> 00:18:14.833
within this one and a half mile circle!

343
00:18:14.899 --> 00:18:17.300
- I see.
- Bunnelby, come on out!

344
00:18:19.899 --> 00:18:22.666
I'd like you to dig a tunnel and find out which direction

345
00:18:22.733 --> 00:18:24.700
the transport machine was heading in.

346
00:18:24.766 --> 00:18:29.933
Bunnel-brrr! Bunnelby!

347
00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:32.166
- That way!
- Got it!

348
00:18:32.233 --> 00:18:34.500
Excellent work, Bunnelby! Lead on!

349
00:18:37.666 --> 00:18:41.166
Well, well, well, it looks like we've finally caught you this time!

350
00:18:41.233 --> 00:18:43.233
- Pikachu!
- Huh?

351
00:18:43.300 --> 00:18:45.800
- Pika!
- That's as far as you go!

352
00:18:45.866 --> 00:18:50.033
How dare you fool me like that? Give back Pikachu right now!

353
00:18:50.100 --> 00:18:52.033
- Inkay!
- Pumpkaboo!

354
00:18:52.100 --> 00:18:53.500
Go!

355
00:18:53.566 --> 00:18:58.000
The future is now, thanks to science! Clemontic Gear on!

356
00:18:58.066 --> 00:19:01.800
Mechanical Absorber of Any Pokémon's Move, model two!

357
00:19:01.866 --> 00:19:03.466
Yeah, go get them, big brother!

358
00:19:03.533 --> 00:19:08.600
- Inkay, Psybeam!
- Inkay!

359
00:19:08.666 --> 00:19:14.066
- Pumpkaboo, Dark Pulse, go!
- Pumpka-ka-ka-ka-ka-ka!

360
00:19:14.133 --> 00:19:15.899
Science is so amazing!

361
00:19:15.966 --> 00:19:19.133
Use Shadow Ball!

362
00:19:22.200 --> 00:19:24.366
Bunnelby, Double Slap!

363
00:19:24.433 --> 00:19:26.466
Bunnelby!

364
00:19:26.533 --> 00:19:29.233
Now use Mud Shot!

365
00:19:29.300 --> 00:19:30.800
Bunnelby!

366
00:19:30.866 --> 00:19:32.233
Argh!

367
00:19:32.300 --> 00:19:36.700
- Ah! Ooh! No, no, no!
- Pik!

368
00:19:36.766 --> 00:19:38.800
Are you okay?

369
00:19:38.866 --> 00:19:41.399
- Pika!
- Great! Use Electro Ball!

370
00:19:48.833 --> 00:19:52.266
The future is not now, thanks to twerps!

371
00:19:52.333 --> 00:19:55.466
- We're blasting off again!
- Inkay!

372
00:19:55.533 --> 00:19:58.766
- Pumpkaboo!
- Wobbuffet!

373
00:19:58.833 --> 00:20:00.200
All right!

374
00:20:00.266 --> 00:20:02.000
Pika!

375
00:20:02.066 --> 00:20:04.766
Thanks a lot, Clemont! You saved the day!

376
00:20:04.833 --> 00:20:09.266
No. In fact, it was all my fault for building that robot.

377
00:20:09.333 --> 00:20:11.133
But it was Team Rocket's fault!

378
00:20:11.200 --> 00:20:13.500
Come on. You didn't do anything wrong!

379
00:20:13.566 --> 00:20:15.733
Really?

380
00:20:15.800 --> 00:20:17.633
Huh?

381
00:20:21.966 --> 00:20:24.433
-Ooh!

382
00:20:24.500 --> 00:20:27.033
Oopsie doops! Are you okay, Clemont?

383
00:20:29.399 --> 00:20:31.433
Although Clemont was tricked into helping Team Rocket

384
00:20:31.500 --> 00:20:34.633
with the robots they used to try to catch Pikachu,

385
00:20:34.700 --> 00:20:38.200
everything worked out in the end, with the help of all our heroes!

386
00:20:38.266 --> 00:20:43.266
Now it's on to Shalour City once again, as the journey continues!
